      "How does an S-Corporation election save self-employment taxes?": "Profits are divided into reasonable W-2 salary and distributions. Distributions are 100% exempt from the 15.3% self-employment tax.",
      "What is the minimum 1099 earnings threshold to trigger self-employment tax?": "You must file Schedule SE and pay self-employment tax if your net profit is $400 or greater in a tax year."
